{"archetypes":[{"name":"path-exhaustion","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"The plan moves three output files into a subdir and lists specific callers to update, but may miss implicit readers outside the scope-file list.","prompt_body":"Verify that the plan accounts for ALL existing references to the three Codex-written output paths — `manifest.json`, `qa-pending.json`, and `codex-impl-transcript.txt` — that currently resolve under `$IMPLEMENT_TMPDIR` root. Check whether any reader or writer in `skills/implement/scripts/`, `scripts/`, or harness files outside the listed scope could silently receive stale (root-level) paths after the subdir move. Confirm that `step-7a.sh` line references in the plan match the actual file structure and that no `.meta` or `.trimmed` derivative paths are overlooked. Flag any plan gap where a file is listed as unchanged but contains a hardcoded path to the old location. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"guard-placement","focus_area":"risk-integration","weight":1,"rationale":"The plan inserts multiple guard blocks at specific line offsets in launch-codex-implement.sh; incorrect placement relative to token rehydration or existing canonicalization could silently skip or double-execute guards.","prompt_body":"Verify that the plan's proposed insertion points in `scripts/launch-codex-implement.sh` — specifically the `_codex_canonical_existing_dir` helper, the FINDING_1 equality guard, the `unset -f _codex_canonical_existing_dir` cleanup, and the transcript-parent parity check — are ordered correctly relative to the existing `IMPLEMENT_TMPDIR` token rehydration block (plan references ~line 127) and the `--add-dir` spawn line (~line 328). Check whether `unset -f` fires before or after the env-var is needed, whether the guard skipping logic (`[[ -n "${IMPLEMENT_TMPDIR:-}" ]]`) correctly handles the harness-without-IMPLEMENT_TMPDIR case, and whether the plan's replacement of lines 110-125 leaves any duplicate or orphaned canonicalization code. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."}]}
